I built the Turkish phone agent for the Freya Bank statement-debt case and saved it under slot `final`. Lint shows 0 errors. I ran one live chat turn, which found a wrong lira reading. I changed the prompt to fix it and saved again, but I haven't run the corrected version.

**The test turn** (customer 95004361, now = 12 Oct 2026 10:30): the agent looked up the card without asking, read the card (Yıldız Premium ending 2000), the statement date, the euro debt, the "no dollar or sterling debt" sentence, the 15 October due date and the extra-transaction offer. All of that matched example 1. The lira line was wrong: it gave 9.500 and 2.000 as the debt and minimum, but the right answer is 12.000 debt and 4.800 minimum, with 9.500 / 2.000 as what is left. The fix tells the agent which service field goes into which part of the sentence and how to decide whether the customer paid nothing, paid below the minimum or paid the minimum.

**How it's built:**
- **Structure:** the date code node runs first, then one main conversation node holding all seven bank tools, then an end node. The call ends when the agent has said a main-menu, human-agent or silence closing sentence. The agent decides that itself and records it in a variable, and the route follows the variable. That is a single node rather than one node per stage, so most rules sit in the prompt instead of in routes and code.
- **Bank services:** every tool calls `https://btb-bank-mock.barsyayc.workers.dev` with the operation's own path from the tool file.
- **Sentences:** the menu's sentences are quoted word for word, along with the ones from the 9 Oct decisions email (silence, off-topic, three tries, transfer to an agent, same-name cards).
- **Rules from the brief in the prompt:**
  - Never say more than the last four digits of a card.
  - Read currency names in full, never the codes.
  - Read one card at a time.
  - Change the statement week only after the preview and an explicit "evet", and only once.
  - Send only the latest statement, only to the registered e-mail, and offer e-mail only when there is one.
  - No transactions on someone else's card.
  - Up to three calming replies to an angry caller before handing over.

**Not done in the time limit:**
- I didn't check the rest of the brief rule by rule against the workflow.
- I only read the brief, the 9 Oct decisions email and the menu prompt sheet. I didn't read the two analysis documents, the meeting transcript, the kickoff email or the service contract text. Any rule only stated there is missing.
- The read-failure handling (try once more, then transfer to an agent) and the e-mail send's failure line are my own wording, not taken from the documents.

