I made two edits to the main prompt and updated the card-number description on the five tools that take it. `out/final.workflow.json` still loads with python3. Nothing was saved to Freya and no eval or chat was run, so these fixes are untested.

The ledger is empty (`tools: []`) in every row of the record, including runs where the agent clearly got bank data: real balances, the registered e-mail address, the 1110 Yıldız Miles debt. So I suspect the "never called" lines are mostly a recording problem. The transcripts do show one real bug behind several of them:
- **The bug:** the bank's card number is masked (`540000******3201`). When a card had to be chosen, or a later card tool was called, the agent sent a wrong card number. It got "not found" back and either wrongly said "Size ait geçerli bir kart bulamadım" or "Şu an sisteme ulaşamıyoruz".
- **The fixes:**
  - The prompt and the tool descriptions now require the full masked string, copied with every asterisk, looked up in the cards list when the caller picks by name or last four. Never just the last four digits.
  - "Size ait geçerli bir kart bulamadım" is now reserved for a cards list with no card.
  - If a card service answers "not found", the agent checks the number against the cards list and calls once more with the exact string.

One line per failure:
- **Tek kart / cards.balance never called:** ignored. The agent read the exact balances, so the call was made and the record simply didn't capture it.
- **Hafta seçimi / statement.week.change never called:** fixed by the card-number rule. The agent's first attempt to read the statement week returned "Şu an sisteme ulaşamıyoruz" for a single-card customer. My guess is the same wrong card number, but I can't confirm it because the record has no tool details.
- **Birkaç kart / cards.list and cards.balance never called:** fixed. After the caller picked Yıldız Premium by name, the balance call failed. The new rule makes the agent send that card's exact masked number. cards.list did run (the agent listed both cards), so that line is a recording gap.
- **Eski ekstre / contact.email.get and statement.pdf.send never called:** ignored. The agent read the registered address before the caller said it and only said "gönderildi" after an explicit yes, so both calls appear to have run. Only the ledger is missing.
- **Bağlı kart / cards.balance, statement.week.get, statement.week.decide never called:** fixed. Picking 3201 returned "no valid card" or "system unreachable", which is the card-number bug. The not-found retry rule and the reserved "no valid card" sentence should stop the false dead end.
- **Geçerli kart bulunamaması / cards.list never called:** ignored. The agent correctly said no valid card was found, which needs cards.list to have run. The behaviour is correct and only the ledger is missing.

